  "title": "Cumulative Loyalty Redemptions by Member Tier",
  "prompt": "The beauty retailer tracks loyalty point redemptions by members across different tier levels (Bronze, Silver, Gold). Management wants to see a running count of redemptions for each member tier, ordered chronologically by redemption date. Write a query that returns each redemption along with a cumulative count of redemptions within that member's tier up to and including that redemption date. Include the redemption_id, member_id, member_tier, redemption_date, points_redeemed, and a column named `cumulative_redemptions_in_tier` showing the running total count. Order the final result by member_tier, then redemption_date, then redemption_id. Note: Some redemptions may occur on the same date within a tier.",
